{# Physical Letters: the recipient reads a delivered letter.  Sent by the plugin with
   PublicSendCustomPromptToLLM; context variables:
     npc             UUID, name of the recipient
     letter          author, recipient, body of the letter being read; read_before is
                     true when the recipient already received this same letter once;
                     can_reply is false when the correspondence has run its course (no reply)
     correspondence  earlier letters between the two that the recipient knows of, oldest
                     first (up to 20): from, to, days_ago, body
     memories        the recipient's other memories most relevant to the writer #}

{# How many of the most recent earlier letters to show. #}
{% set max_earlier_letters = 5 %}

{% set actor = decnpc(npc.UUID) %}
{% set first_earlier_letter = length(correspondence) - max_earlier_letters %}
[ system ]
    You are helping {{ actor.name }} read a letter that has just been delivered to {{ actor.objectivePronoun }}. You capture how {{ actor.name }} truly reacts to it, what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} will remember of it, and whether {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} writes back, staying true to {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} personality, background and speech patterns.

    {{ render_character_profile("full", npc.UUID) }}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
    {% if correspondence and length(correspondence) > 0 %}
    ## Earlier Letters Between {{ actor.name }} and {{ letter.author }}
    {% for earlier in correspondence %}
    {% if loop.index >= first_earlier_letter %}
    From {{ earlier.from }} to {{ earlier.to }}, {% if earlier.days_ago == 0 %}earlier today{% else if earlier.days_ago == 1 %}a day ago{% else %}{{ earlier.days_ago }} days ago{% endif %}:
    ```
    {{ earlier.body }}
    ```
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    ## The Letter
    From: {{ letter.author }}
    To: {{ letter.recipient }}

    ```
    {{ letter.body }}
    ```
    {% if letter.read_before %}

    {{ actor.name }} has received this very letter before, word for word{% if correspondence and length(correspondence) > 0 %}; any reply {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} sent to it is among the earlier letters above{% endif %}. {{ letter.author }} has sent it again.
    {% endif %}

    {% if memories and length(memories) > 0 %}
    ## What {{ actor.name }} Remembers That May Bear on It
    {% for memory in memories -%}
    - {{ memory }}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    ## Instructions

    1. **React in character.** Decide how {{ actor.name }} feels on reading the letter, given {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} personality and history with {{ letter.author }}: warmly, coldly, with suspicion, indifference or anything in between. Not everyone is glad to receive a letter.

    {% if letter.can_reply %}
    2. **Decide whether {{ actor.name }} replies.** Someone close to {{ letter.author }}, or with something to say, usually does; a stranger, a busy or proud person, or someone who resents {{ letter.author }} may not.
    {% else %}
    2. **{{ actor.name }} doesn't reply this time**: the exchange has run its course for now. Set 'reply' to false and 'reply_text' to "".
    {% endif %}

    3. **If {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} replies, write the reply** as a letter in {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} own voice: addressed to {{ letter.author }}, answering what the letter said, a few short paragraphs at most, signed with {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} name. {{ actor.name }} can only write about what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} knows; don't invent events in {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} life. If there are earlier letters, this is a correspondence: answer what is new, stay consistent with what was already written, and don't repeat it.{% if letter.read_before %} Receiving the same letter twice is odd: {{ actor.name }} notices, may be puzzled, amused or irritated, and need not answer it all over again.{% endif %}

    4. **Write the memory {{ actor.name }} keeps of this**, in first person as {{ actor.name }}, two to four sentences: that a letter came from {{ letter.author }}, what it said in brief, how {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} felt about it, and whether {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} wrote back and what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} said.

    **IMPORTANT**: Return ONLY a valid JSON object. Do not include explanatory text before or after the JSON.

    Return JSON with exactly these fields:
    - 'memory': the first-person memory described above (string)
    - 'emotion': {{ actor.name }}'s main feeling on reading the letter, one word (e.g. "touched", "annoyed", "wary", "glad")
    - 'importance': how much the letter matters to {{ actor.name }} (0.0-1.0 float)
    - 'reply': true if {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} writes back, false if not
    - 'reply_text': the reply letter, or "" if {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} doesn't write back
[ end user ]
